const sections=[['What is Homo Faber?','Homo Faber is an international biennial dedicated to excellence in contemporary craftsmanship. The 2026 edition brings together hundreds of handmade objects by artisans and creators from around the world.'],['An Island of Light','Under the artistic direction of Es Devlin, the fourth edition explores the relationship between light, materials and the human hand. Fifteen immersive installations unfold through the historic spaces and gardens of Fondazione Giorgio Cini.'],['More than an exhibition','The programme includes live demonstrations, participatory workshops, culinary experiences and special tours, allowing visitors to discover not only finished objects but also the skills, gestures and processes behind them.'],['San Giorgio Maggiore','The island is only a few minutes by vaporetto from St Mark’s Square, yet feels much quieter. Combine Homo Faber with the Basilica of San Giorgio Maggiore and the exceptional view across the Bacino di San Marco.'],['Homo Faber in Città','The project also extends across Venice with exhibitions and initiatives dedicated to craft, design, materials and local makers, offering another way to discover places beyond the classic visitor routes.'],['Practical information','Homo Faber 2026 runs from 1 to 30 September at Fondazione Giorgio Cini. Opening times, tickets, workshops and the daily programme may change, so always check the official website before visiting.']];
